      "seq": 48,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791901932122,
      "reason": "Picking the most frequent pair no longer runs a Python-level key function or comprehension for every pair. In BasicTokenizer.train and RegexTokenizer.train, the counts are copied into a list once. max, list.count and list.index then run in C, and the pair is taken from list(stats) at the first maximal position. This is the same first-maximum choice that max(stats, key=stats.get) makes. When counts tie in RegexTokenizer.train, the exact pair-to-chunks index (`where`) gives the earliest chunk that holds a tied pair. Only that chunk is scanned, so the winner is the same as before: the first tied pair in chunk order. Outputs are byte-identical. Measured train_ir ratio 0.9796."
    }
